---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
---

<section class="box skills">
	<div class="stack gap-2 lg:gap-4">
		<Icon
			icon="terminal-window"
			color="var(--accent-regular)"
			size="2.5rem"
			gradient
		/>
		<h2>Backend Engineering</h2>
		<p>
			Java and Spring Boot in production — designing APIs, services, and data
			flows that hold up under real-world load and complexity.
		</p>
	</div>
	<div class="stack gap-2 lg:gap-4">
		<Icon icon="trophy" color="var(--accent-regular)" size="2.5rem" gradient />
		<h2>From Code to Cluster</h2>
		<p>
			Comfortable across the stack, from Spring Boot services to Kubernetes
			clusters and GitOps pipelines with Flux and Kustomize.
		</p>
	</div>
	<div class="stack gap-2 lg:gap-4">
		<Icon
			icon="strategy"
			color="var(--accent-regular)"
			size="2.5rem"
			gradient
		/>
		<h2>Collaborative by Default</h2>
		<p>
			I've always gravitated toward the parts of engineering that involve
			working with people — explaining tradeoffs, aligning teams, and making
			complexity feel manageable.
		</p>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.box {
		border: 1px solid var(--gray-800);
		border-radius: 0.75rem;
		padding: 1.5rem;
		background-color: var(--gray-999_40);
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
	}

	.skills {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 3rem;
	}

	.skills h2 {
		font-size: var(--text-lg);
	}

	.skills p {
		color: var(--gray-400);
	}

	@media (min-width: 50em) {
		.box {
			border-radius: 1.5rem;
			padding: 2.5rem;
		}

		.skills {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
			gap: 5rem;
		}

		.skills h2 {
			font-size: var(--text-2xl);
		}
	}
</style>
